TYPES.md §3.5, §5.1, STDLIB.md §4.1, §5, DECISIONS 317, 456: evaluation agrees with the checker in key and element positions. `xs.k` on a list keyed by a ref whose leaf is a String (`ts`, `us` at 2 levels) or a table id (`ps`) is the entry with key `k`, and a key no entry has is E4002 there. A named argument of contains, indexOf, get, find and hasKey is the positional one. An index of context-dependent arithmetic is an Int position of a plain list (`xs[1 + 1]`) and an Int key of a keyed list (`js[1 + 9]`). On `picked`, keyed by a ref into `pool`, a table of its own element type, an element is tested with `in` and a key with hasKey; `picked.a` (its entry, a String-leaf `.k`) is in it, `pool.a` (an entry of pool, another identity, TYPES.md §6.3, §7.5) is not.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

